{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJqabyCBeoDuirBZMGBR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full suite is running with buffered output; I'll be notified when it completes. \n\nSummary of where things stand while I wait for the final gate:\n\n**WI-272 — Dashboard work-item status fidelity** — the uncommitted work from session 001 is complete and I've verified it end-to-end:\n\n- **Root cause fixed:** `deferred`/`blocked` were absent from `STATUS_FILL`, so `_wi_st()` clamped both to `queued`. They're now keyed with distinct, accessible fills (`#6b21a8` deferred 8.7:1, `#b91c1c` blocked 6.5:1 on white text — both clear WCAG AA).\n- **All four named surfaces + legend preserve the true status:** label glyphs (`▽`/`◼`), the detail JSON (`\"status\"`), accessible node/tooltip titles (`(deferred)`/`(blocked)`), and the DAG legend.\n- **Anti-recurrence:** the JS `statusColor` map is now emitted from `STATUS_FILL` (was a hand-kept four-state copy — the actual M-2 defect vector), plus a drift-guard test asserting `STATUS_FILL`/`STATUS_GLYPH` stay a bijection with `check_trajectory.KNOWN_STATUSES`.\n\nVerified so far: the 3 targeted tests pass, ruff format+lint clean, the full `test_gen_trajectory.py` module (100 tests incl. all WCAG/glyph/bijection invariants) passes. The SR-053 render critique (independent, \"never the authoring build\") and the `PROJECT_STATE.html` regeneration are correctly out of the build worker's scope — the integrator and a separate critique session own those. The untracked 001 iteration log is harness telemetry, so my commit will stage only the two source files.\n\nOnce the full unfiltered suite comes back green I'll commit with the WI trailers."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":275,"cache_read_input_tokens":125223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":275},